{% set order = ["Critical", "High", "Medium", "Low"] %}
{% set counts = [] %}
{% for sev in order %}{% set _ = counts.append(findings | selectattr("severity", "equalto", sev) | list | length) %}{% endfor %}
# Security Findings

## All findings

| ID | Severity | Finding |
|----|----------|---------|
{% for f in findings -%}
| {{ f.id }} | {{ f.severity }} | {{ f.text }} |
{% endfor %}

## Count by severity

The rows are grouped in the template with Jinja's `selectattr` filter.

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
{% for sev in order -%}
| {{ sev }} | {{ counts[loop.index0] }} |
{% endfor %}| **Total** | **{{ findings | length }}** |

## Chart

The same grouping fed into a native `graph` block. The `x` labels and `Count`
values are emitted as JSON with the `tojson` filter.

```graph
{
  "title": "Findings by severity",
  "show_legend": false,
  "data": {
    "x": {{ order | tojson }},
    "Count": {{ counts | tojson }}
  },
  "series": [
    { "label": "Count", "type": "bar", "colour": "#c0392b" }
  ]
}
```
